    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d56-a14">

                <pb facs="0120" n="70" xml:id="pg70"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">note of the portuguese legation to the brazilian
                        government.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Petropolis</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-04-02"><hi rendition="#italic">April 2,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Confirming the information which I gave you on last Thursday, I have the honor to
                    assure you, being duly authorized, that His Majesty’s Government has given the
                    necessary orders that the Brazilian insurgents, in refuge on board the
                    Portuguese men of war, shall be landed as soon as possible on Portuguese soil,
                    where they will be placed under military guard by the competent authorities, and
                    will not be allowed to interfere with the political movements in Brazil. I hope
                    that this attitude of the Portuguese Government, harmonizing the duties of a
                    friendly power, entirely neutral in the civil war, with the sacred principles of
                    international law of all civilized nations, will contribute to further bind the
                    cordial relations existing between Brazil and Portugal, which is so much to be
                    desired for the interests of both nations.</p>
                <p>I take the occasion, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Conde de Paraty.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
